 flood has now severed the only road  out of bahrain the river shifted its  position  the locals crisscrossed the torrent on  rickety bridges and even more perilous  cable trolleys  we met shamshire in the remains of her  home she is 105 years old  like so many here she believes the  changing weather  her centenarian husband cherry gull  agrees with his  [Music]  i wouldn't give wife no revenue  amid the destruction families adapt to  the new shape of their town  washing in the midst of the newly  arrived boulders  but the real priority here is to  redirect the river and to start building  bridges and repairing roads heading  north everything beyond this point is  destroyed  people have scattered from that side  because no lanka or  bridges or all languages are washed away  by the flood but the alhamdulillah local  people are helped each other a little  bit  but the relief is not enough for us we  need  a lot of  foods items medicines and such more  items for home shelters etc that that  will be a little bit good for us  neither faith or resolve can be doubted  in pakistan  but this is simply overwhelming and they  desperately need help  stuart ramsey sky news bahrain in the  swap valley
 

